invariant: INV-75
file: proof/run.sh
catches: test/prove-status-check.sh
reason: a job that wrote no status takes wait's answer, so a job a signal
  ended after cbmc printed VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL passes when wait
  answers 0 for another process. The check runs such a job with wait
  answering 0 and requires FAILED.

--- old
        if [ "$rc" -eq 0 ]; then rc=1; fi
        ;;
--- new
        ;;
